# A shell script checked out with CRLF is a broken shell script: bash reads the
# carriage return as part of the command, and a test that looks for a line of
# install.sh does not find it. Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true, so the
# windows-latest runner was checking out scripts/install.sh with CRLF and the
# ordering assertions failed on a file that is correct in the repository.
# Say it once here instead of in every reader.
*.sh text eol=lf
